# Sightline BDR Alignment

Companion to `specs-and-adrs-before-code.mdc`, `style-css-cache-bust.mdc`, and `button-section-contrast.mdc`. Read those for full detail; this rule adds the **done** gate.

## Before visual, copy, or IA changes

1. Read `sightline-brand-system/AGENTS.md` and relevant locked BDRs in `sightline-brand-system/bdr/`.
2. **Never edit a locked BDR body** — create a superseding BDR; set `superseded_by:` on the old file's frontmatter only.
3. Untraceable tokens, colors, or copy → log in `sightline-brand-system/spec/04-provenance-debt-log.md` (do not silently default).

## CSS and cache bust

Follow `style-css-cache-bust.mdc`. Any `style.css` change → increment `?v=` in **every** HTML page that links it:

- `index.html`
- `design-system/index.html`
- `sightline/index.html`
- `sightline-lived-out/index.html`
- `seam-field-guide/index.html`
- `verdict/index.html`
- `verdict/mca/index.html`

Keep the same version across all pages.

## CTAs on colored sections

Follow `button-section-contrast.mdc` (BDR-0023): filled CTA background must not match the parent section surface. On `--c-deep` sections use `.on-deep` or documented section-scoped overrides — not default `.btn-primary`.

## Specs and ADRs

Follow `specs-and-adrs-before-code.mdc` for `docs/specs/` and ADR alignment on implementation changes.

## Before considering CSS/governance work done

Run `npm run validate` or `node scripts/validate-alignment.js`. Fix all errors; address warnings or log provenance debt.
